    "created_at": "2016-06-06T18:09:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-06T18:09:58Z",
    "body": "> unload event is not working. It is usefull for saving state in server before of unloading\n\nSo, this is a feature request to add unload to worker code (or maybe just shared worker code). Tagging as needs-implementer-interest. I tentatively agree that saving state is a reasonable use case, although unload events have caused a lot of pain in documents, so it might be better to explore other solutions.\n\n> message channel port has not onclose event. It is difficult to keep the state of clients connected. \n\nThis is https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=28813. Unfortunately it is harder than it seems.\n\n> shared worker seams not working if you reload a single page. When browser is opening a page in a domain X and then user reload , coming from same domain, it might reuse the same shared worker. In this way in the case of realoading the same page , it works. \n\nI'm not sure what you mean by \"not work\" here.\n",
