    "body": "https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=28813. that developer is discussing about nothing. \nwhen a client close a port in a direction ... in the opposite direction i throws a event onclose. It is very simple. \nThey can add also this object extends Closeable object. So browser know it has to call close() if it is not did before programmatically. They havent to invent anything ... they have just to copy what is already working in java and paste in javascript.\n",
